    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed development, by reason of the proposed first-floor side and rear extension\r\nin conjunction with the proposed gable end roof and rear dormer, would give\r\nrise to an unsympathetic, incongruous, bulky, obtrusive and contrived form of\r\ndevelopment which would fail to respect the scale, character, massing,\r\ncomposition and design of the host and neighbouring properties, to the\r\ndetriment of the character and appearance of the subject dwellinghouse and the\r\nvisual amenities of the area, contrary to the high quality design aspirations\r\nof National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 D.1, D.11, D.12 of the\r\nLondon Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1 (B) of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012),\r\npolicy DM 1 of the Harrow Development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
